            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. When an emergency situation arises which could not be anticipated in advance, an extended duty assignment beyond the regular duty day may be made. When such an assignment becomes necessary, volunteers shall be utilized first. When no volunteers are available, priority consideration shall be given to teachers' personal commitments which cannot be re-scheduled. The teacher assigned on said extended duty shall be allowed to take an equal amount of compensatory time during non-student contact time to be taken within ten (10) duty days or at a time mutually agreeable to the teacher and the principal.",
